> Fubini's algorithm looks like this:
>
> 1. Search the whole dungeon and collect every stackable weapon you see.
> Put them all in a big pile and cancel them.  Select the stack with the
> largest number of items (probably arrows or darts).
> 2. Enchant the whole stack to +7 and fooproof them.
> 3. Take HALF of the stack and attempt to enchant it to +8.  If it fails,
> and the weapons evaporate, then try again, taking HALF of the remainder,
> and so on, until you succeed.
> 4. You now have some (probably smaller) number of weapons, half of which
> are +7 and half +8.  Take all of the remaining +7 weapons and attempt to
> enchant them to +8.
> 5. Now you have a (probably even smaller) number of weapons, all at +8.
> Repeat steps 3 and 4 to get some of them to +9.
